.docs/


# ── Rust ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Slashless siblings matter: worktrees created by the worktree-setup sync engine
# SYMLINK these caches to the main checkout, and git treats a symlink as a file,
# so a trailing-slash pattern does not match it. Without both forms a `git add -A`
# in a worktree commits symlinks pointing at absolute paths on one machine.
/target/
/target
**/target/
**/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw
*.profdata
/.cargo/.global-cache
/.cargo/.package-cache
/.cargo/.package-cache-mutate
/.cargo/registry/


# ── Node / TypeScript build artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────
# Slashless siblings cover the worktree cache symlinks (see the Rust block above).
node_modules/
node_modules
.next/
.next
*.tsbuildinfo
packages/*/vendor/

# ── Repo-specific ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/
proxies/
outputs/
/dist/
/dist
/.zcode/
config.local.toml
*.key
*.pem
*.cert

